# Participant material must never enter Git, on any branch.
# Policy: docs/participant-material-policy.md
#
# This is a safety net, not the control. The control is the checklist in
# CONTRIBUTING.md and not putting such files in the working tree at all.
# It only stops an accident; it cannot stop a deliberate `git add -f`.
#
# Patterns are kept TARGETED on purpose. An earlier version matched the bare
# substring *transcript*, which also blocked a page called
# transcription-and-burden.md — a lexical net wide enough to catch the
# accident is wide enough to hide legitimate work on transcription and
# transcriptomics, and a rule that silently drops wanted files stops being
# trusted. Directory and format patterns catch the realistic accident, which
# is a folder of transcripts dropped into the tree.

# Directories that would hold participant material
transcripts/
**/transcripts/
participant-data/
judging-notes/
curation-notes/
submissions/

# Caption and subtitle formats
*.vtt
*.srt
*.sbv
*.ttml

# Archives dropped into the tree while working
*.zip
*.tar.gz
